[%think 36509] [%out 36981] [%in 2] [%cacheread 0] [%cachewrite 2217] **Black's
threats right now:** - **Rook takes bishop with check (f2xe2).** The rook on e2
checks along the open e-file, and nothing of mine protects e2. - **Rook takes
advisor with check (f2xf0).** The cannon on h0 screens over my bishop on g0 to
protect f0. My king cannot recapture and has almost no escape squares. -
**Cannon takes pawn with check (b3xe3).** My knight on c2 simply takes the
cannon on e3, so this one is not a real threat. **Candidates I rejected:** -
**Knight moves (c2e1 / c2d0 / c2b0).** These expose my rook's side to attack.
After c2e1, black mates at once with f2xf0. - **Rook d8→d7 to fork knight and
bishop.** Black's advisor on e8 just captures the rook on d7. - **Cannon
b2→b0.** The king would act as the cannon's screen to defend f0. But after
f2xe2+ I still lose the bishop, then the e3 pawn, and the knight on c2 would be
loose. **Choice: king to e1 (帅五进一).** - The king now guards e2, so f2xe2+
is met by king takes rook. - f2xf0 is no longer check. I lose only one advisor
and get a free tempo afterwards. - b3xe3+ is still answered by knight c2 takes
e3. } 车６进２ 22. 车六平七 { [%emt 0:03:55] [%think 21542] [%out 21886]
